  Thursday — Add Agentic Behavior (Tool Use)

  1.5 hrs

  Upgrade to agent.py — give the LLM tools it can choose to call:
  from langchain_community.llms import Ollama
  from langchain.agents import AgentExecutor, create_react_agent
  from langchain.tools import Tool
  from langchain import hub

  llm = Ollama(model="llama3.2")

  # Tool 1: Search your documents
  def search_docs(query):
      return qa_chain.invoke(query)["result"]

  # Tool 2: Simple calculator
  def calculate(expression):
      return str(eval(expression))

  tools = [
      Tool(name="DocumentSearch", func=search_docs,
           description="Search HR and IT policy documents"),
      Tool(name="Calculator", func=calculate,
           description="Perform calculations"),
  ]

  # ReAct agent — this is the agentic loop
  prompt = hub.pull("hwchase17/react")
  agent = create_react_agent(llm, tools, prompt)
  executor = AgentExecutor(agent=agent, tools=tools, verbose=True)

  result = executor.invoke({"input": "What is the IT helpdesk number?"})
  print(result["output"])

  Run it with verbose=True — watch the agent think step by step. That IS the ReAct loop.

